From efb5e91e2e7a65a590505490f4e157f3da5a212a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:18:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stage: profile morph panel, inline settings, working
 background, Glasmio text editing

- Profile: the button now morphs into an Edit Profile panel (GlasmioMenu with custom content) and
  collapses back into the same button. Settings opens only after the collapse finishes. The old
  separate dialog, which had no exit animation, is gone.
- Navbar and profile button fade with CompositingStrategy.ModulateAlpha so the glass shadow/rim is
  no longer cropped by an offscreen layer and nothing pops when alpha returns to 1.
- Settings: theme, accent swatches, text size, card transparency, UI style and the background
  controls are live inside their rows; no more tap-through sub pages.
- Background: choosing a photo / gradient / plain now writes bgStyle together with the photo.
  The app root only paints a photo while bgStyle is Custom, so picking one used to change nothing.
- Text input: GlasmioTextSelectionHost at the root and a new XvoxTextInput (GlasmioEditableText)
  replace BasicTextField in 10 places; the library-filter Material field uses GlasmioTextField.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KievH9end6o7BBBHs4s3kc
